---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../lib";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Leat Consulting is run by Fraser Davidson, a platform engineer with over ten years of experience building and securing infrastructure in financial services, retail and the public sector."
>
  <h1>About Leat Consulting</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Leat Consulting is run by Fraser Davidson, a platform engineer with over ten years of experience
    building and securing infrastructure in financial services, retail and the public sector.
  </p>

  <h2>Experience</h2>
  <p>
    Most recently Fraser has been a senior platform engineer at a quantitative trading firm, moving its
    core engineering tools (source control, CI, artefact storage and secrets management) to AWS and
    Kubernetes, with every piece of infrastructure defined in Terraform.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before that, as a cloud consultant, he worked with tier 1 banks and large enterprises. That included
    self-service account provisioning and compliance tooling across thousands of AWS accounts, and a
    serverless data platform for a bank, hardened alongside its security team and handed over with
    training.
  </p>
  <p>
    Earlier he led infrastructure and DevOps for a UK retailer, taking it from hand-built servers to
    infrastructure as code, CI/CD and Kubernetes, and worked on PCI-compliant e-commerce in New Zealand.
  </p>
  <p>
    He is a HashiCorp Certified Terraform Associate and a Microsoft Certified Azure Administrator, and
    holds a BSc (Hons) in Finance and Economics from the University of Canterbury.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>We show our own work. Our pipelines and the rules that protect them are public.</li>
    <li>We work through pull requests in your repositories, so your team sees and approves every change.</li>
    <li>We hand over. You own what we deliver, and your team can run it without us.</li>
    <li>We are plain about trade-offs, including when the simpler option is the right one.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="cta"><a class="button" href={href("contact/")}>Get in touch</a></p>
</Base>
